\DOC FULL_UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC

\TYPE {FULL_UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal whose conclusion equates a concrete event-trace expression with
an application of a trace-defining function.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. Applied to a goal {A ?- t = u} where {t} is a
built-up event list (lists, {CONS}/{APPEND} combinations, possibly containing
embedded applications of other trace functions) and {u} is an application of a
trace function to arguments, it discharges the goal entirely; the assumptions
{A} are neither extended nor reduced.
{
   A ?- t = u
   ==========  FULL_UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC
               (no subgoals)
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the outcome is this complete discharge of the goal, and
every input is an equation of this event-list form appearing among large
symbolic-execution assumption lists.

\ENDDOC
